{"key": "c44050169ddb7c9b", "role": "operator", "t": 1790994973.163, "seconds": 5.667, "output": "```python\ndef check_similarity(PURPOSE, Amount):\n    if isinstance(PURPOSE, str) and isinstance(Amount, str):\n        if 'loan' in PURPOSE.lower() and 'loan' in Amount.lower():\n            return 1\n        elif 'credit' in PURPOSE.lower() and 'credit' in Amount.lower():\n            return 1\n        else:\n            return 0\n    elif isinstance(PURPOSE, dict) and isinstance(Amount, dict):\n        if PURPOSE.get('feature') == Amount.get('feature'):\n            return 1\n        else:\n            return 0\n    else:\n        return 0\n\n# Test the function\nprint(check_similarity('loan', 'loan'))  # Expected output: 1\nprint(check_similarity('credit', 'credit'))  # Expected output: 1\nprint(check_similarity('loan', 'credit'))  # Expected output: 0\nprint(check_similarity({'feature': 'loan'}, {'feature': 'loan'}))  # Expected output: 1\nprint(check_similarity({'feature': 'loan'}, {'feature': 'credit'}))  # Expected output: 0\n```"}
